  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Loba. South American Rummy. 2-5 players, 108 cards (2 decks + 4 Jokers). Deal 11 each. Draw from stock or discard. Meld sets (3+ same rank) and sequences (3+ consecutive same suit). Jokers wild. Can lay off on any meld. Discard to end turn. Go out to end round. Penalties: Joker=50, Ace=20, Face=10, Others=face value. Lowest total wins.',
    Player: "Welcome to Loba! You're playing with two decks plus Jokersâ€”108 cards total. Form sets (same rank) and sequences (same suit, consecutive) to meld. Jokers are wild but cost 50 points if you're caught with one! Get rid of all your cards to go out and stick your opponents with penalty points. Â¡Buena suerte!",
    objective: "Form all cards in your hand into valid melds and 'go out' (empty your hand). Lowest cumulative score across all rounds wins.",
    gameplay: "1. **Draw**: On your turn, draw one card from the stock or take the top card from the discard pile. 2. **Melding**: You can lay down melds as soon as you have them. In the first round, you usually need a minimum 'opening' count (e.g., 30 or 40 points in some variants). 3. **Laying Off**: You can add cards to your own or opponents' existing melds on the table. 4. **Discard**: End your turn by discarding one card to the discard pile.",
    keyRules: [
      'Juego (Set): 3+ cards of same rank (different suits).',
      'Escalera (Sequence): 3+ consecutive cards of same suit.',
      'Jokers and sometimes 2s act as wildcards.',
      'Sequence cannot consist solely of wildcards.',
      'Must draw before melding or laying off.',
      'Must end turn with a discard (unless going out).',
      "Can lay off on opponents' melds once you've opened.",
      'Going out ends the round; remaining cards count as penalties.',
    ],
